//! # Compile-time inputs and source generation
//!
//! Hew provides bounded syntax macros, package-confined compile-time inputs,
//! and manifest-controlled source generation. They run at different stages and
//! carry different authority.
//!
//! `include_str!("path")` and `include_bytes!("path")` embed a package file.
//! `embed!("data.json")` decodes JSON, YAML, or TOML into its expected concrete
//! type. `stringify!(expression)` returns canonical source without resolving or
//! evaluating the expression, and `location!()` returns a package-relative
//! source location. File paths cannot escape the package after symlink
//! resolution.
//!
//! A declarative `macro` matches token trees and produces expressions or
//! items. Captured identifiers keep the caller's context; introduced bindings
//! are fresh and free names resolve in the defining module. Expansion is
//! bounded and cannot run code, inspect types, read files, or use the network.
//! Built-in input operations retain the explicit file authority described
//! above. Use `hew tool expand file.hew` to inspect expanded syntax.
//!
//! Custom attributes are attribute-macro rules and must resolve after macro
//! expansion. Unknown attributes are errors. Built-ins include resource and
//! wire markers, test and benchmark markers, actor lifecycle hooks,
//! `#[every(...)]`, `#[intercept]`, `#[confined]`, and native-boundary
//! attributes; each is accepted only on its documented declaration kind.
//!
//! `[[generate]]` entries in `hew.toml` name ordered, deterministic source
//! generation steps with declared input globs and one owned output directory.
//! `hew generate` runs stale steps; check, build, run, and test prepare them
//! before loading generated modules. `hew generate --check` regenerates in
//! scratch space and fails on a diff. Generated `.hew` files are formatted and
//! published with the package; registry dependencies never execute generators.
//!
//! Generation limits filesystem writes to the declared output, refuses
//! network, process, environment, and native-package authority, fixes clocks,
//! and seeds randomness. This makes generation reproducible, but it is not an
//! operating-system sandbox.
